Run an Apache Kafka performance test and enforce an **A–F** SLA grade gate in GitHub Actions with [Kates](https://github.com/bmscomp/kates).

The action installs the `kates` CLI (when not already on `PATH`), runs `kates gate -o json` against a reachable Kates API, exposes the run's grade and verdict as step outputs, writes a Markdown SLA summary table to `$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY`, and exits non-zero when the grade falls below `min-grade`.

## Usage

```yaml
steps:
  - name: Run Kafka SLA Quality Gate
    id: kafka-gate
    uses: bmscomp/kates@__TAG__
    with:
      api-url: http://localhost:8080
      api-key: ${{ secrets.KATES_API_KEY }}
      min-grade: B
      type: LOAD
      records: 100000
      timeout: 180
```

## Inputs

| Input | Default | Description |
|:------|:--------|:------------|
| `api-url` | `http://localhost:8080` | URL of the Kates API |
| `api-key` | `""` | API key for the Kates API (from Secret `kates-api-key`) |
| `min-grade` | `C` | Minimum passing performance grade (`A`, `B`, `C`, `D`, or `F`) |
| `type` | `LOAD` | Workload type (`LOAD`, `STRESS`, `SPIKE`, `ENDURANCE`, `VOLUME`, `CAPACITY`, `ROUND_TRIP`, `INTEGRITY`) |
| `records` | `50000` | Number of records to produce |
| `backend` | `""` | Benchmark backend (`native` or `trogdor`) |
| `timeout` | `180` | Timeout in seconds |
| `version` | `latest` | Kates CLI release tag to install (`latest` or a tag such as `__TAG__`) |

## Outputs

| Output | Description |
|:-------|:------------|
| `run-id` | ID of the test run created by `kates gate` |
| `grade` | Computed `A–F` performance grade |
| `passed` | Whether the run met or exceeded `min-grade` (`true` or `false`) |

## Grading Thresholds

| Grade | Minimum Avg Throughput | Maximum P99 Latency |
|:------|:-----------------------|:--------------------|
| **A** | `>= 50,000 rec/s` | `< 5 ms` |
| **B** | `>= 30,000 rec/s` | `< 20 ms` |
| **C** | `>= 15,000 rec/s` | `< 50 ms` |
| **D** | `>= 5,000 rec/s` | `< 200 ms` |
| **F** | Below grade D thresholds | `>= 200 ms` |

## Install the `kates` CLI (`__TAG__`)

```bash
# Homebrew (macOS & Linux)
brew install bmscomp/tap/kates

# Direct binary archive (__TAG__)
curl -fsSL https://github.com/bmscomp/kates/releases/download/__TAG__/kates-$(uname -s | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')-$(uname -m | sed 's/x86_64/amd64/;s/aarch64/arm64/').tar.gz | tar -xz
```

